 roleInSystem:"Moves finished medicines from manufacturers' C&F agents through stockists and distributors to roughly 12 lakh retail chemists, hospital pharmacies and e-pharmacies. Trade margins are capped by regulation (typically ~10% for wholesalers and ~20% for retailers on scheduled drugs).",
 whyItMatters:"India's medicine distribution is still highly fragmented. Organised chains (Apollo Pharmacy, MedPlus) and consolidators (Entero, Keimed) are taking share by offering reliable supply, private-label generics and digital ordering - a scale game with thin margins but large revenue and real network effects.",
 valuePoolDescription:"High-volume, low-margin: distributors earn ~3-5% EBITDA and chains ~5-9%, so profitability depends on store maturity, private-label mix and working capital. Private-label generics can earn several times the margin of branded resale, which is why every chain pushes them.",
 bottlenecks:["Regulated trade margins limit pricing", "Working-capital intensity (inventory and stockist credit)", "Unregulated e-pharmacy rules and pushback from chemist associations (AIOCD)"],
